ian because it was akin to the native idiom of the Greek-speaking population in the Argead Kingdom. borrowed as Ancient Macedonian [script needed] (*mīrýkhā) * Proto-Albanian *brukā. Compare Prot"},{"parola":"harlis","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"or from","significato":"to bring into high spirits (of a horse)","termine_origine":"*χαραλίζω","termine_origine_traslitterazione":"*kharalízō","catena":[{"codice":"grc-dor","nome":"Doric Greek","termine":"*χαραλίζω","traslitterazione":"*kharalízō","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"grc-dor","ambiti":[],"via":"","alternative":[{"codice":"grc-dor","nome":"Doric Greek","termine":"*χαραλίζω","traslitterazione":"*kharalízō","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"χαρίζομαι","traslitterazione":"kharízomai","categoria":"prestito"}],"testo":"Borrowed from Doric Greek *χαραλίζω (*kharalízō) from Ancient Greek χαρίζομαι (kharízomai) or from harlë."},{"parola":"mollë","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"either","significato":"apple","termine_origine":"","catena":[{"codice":"grc-dor","nome":"Doric Greek","termine":"","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"grc-dor","ambiti":["cucina"],"via":"","alternative":[{"codice":"sqj-pro","nome":"Proto-Albanian","termine":"*mālā","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"grc-dor","nome":"Doric Greek","termine":"","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"","categoria":"latinismo_dotto"}],"testo":"From Proto-Albanian *mālā, akin to Ancient Greek μῆλον (mêlon, “apple”), Latin mālum (“apple”), either a cognate or borrowed from either of the two. Likely from a western dialect borrowed from Doric Greek. A borrowing from Latin would be unusually early, as the shift from *ā to o, characteristic of "},{"parola":"tarogzë","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Uncertain; alternatively; modello unc/uncertain","significato":"helmet","termine_origine":"θωράκειον","termine_origine_traslitterazione":"thōrákeion","catena":[{"codice":"grc-dor","nome":"Doric Greek","termine":"θωράκειον","traslitterazione":"thōrákeion","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc-dor","ambiti":[],"via":"","alternative":[{"codice":"grc-dor","nome":"Doric Greek","termine":"θωράκειον","traslitterazione":"thōrákeion","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gkm","nome":"Byzantine Greek","termine":"θώραξ","traslitterazione":"thṓrax","categoria":"prestito"}],"testo":"Uncertain. According to Çabej, the word is attested in Pult. It could be an early borrowing from Doric Greek θωράκειον (thōrákeion) or θωράκιον (thōrákion), a diminutive of θώραξ (thṓrax, “breastplate, cuirass, corselet”), or directly from the latter. Alternatively, it could be a later loan from Byz"}]}